# Testing

- Framework: Minitest (not RSpec). Use factories over fixtures except for static files (or binary fixtures) when needed.
- Descriptions/names: always English, in simple quotes.
- System tests: Capybara only when necessary (slow/flaky); favor faster layers (model, service, controller, component tests).
- System tests: do not launch a full file test suite in the terminal. Tests are slow, run it one by one.
- Cover happy path + main failure modes; avoid exhaustive edge-case archaeology unless the bug demands it.
- Shoulda: use `setup` / `context` (and matchers) to DRY structured tests and scope related tests together. Prefer `should '...' do` over `test '...' do`.
- Aim for solid coverage on components, concerns, helpers, decorators, but keep tests simple and fast.
